WEBVTT

00:00.000 --> 00:03.600
Hi, I'm Jonah, one of the co-founders here at VoiceOS,

00:03.700 --> 00:05.900
and here's a quick overview on how to use it.

00:06.000 --> 00:08.900
So we have two different modes, Dictation Mode and Agent Mode.

00:09.400 --> 00:12.700
Dictation Mode essentially lets you speak naturally, make a bunch of mistakes,

00:12.800 --> 00:16.400
and it will polish the text and format it anywhere you can type.

00:16.500 --> 00:18.400
Let me give an example.

00:18.500 --> 00:21.500
So I could be here in Google Chrome or Gmail,

00:21.600 --> 00:24.500
and instead of drafting and typing out the draft for the email,

00:24.600 --> 00:27.900
I could simply hold fn and speak naturally.

00:28.300 --> 00:30.900
Hi Kai, do you have time to meet tomorrow for some coffee at 6pm?

00:31.000 --> 00:34.000
Oh sorry, I mean 7pm. Best, Jonah.

00:37.200 --> 00:40.400
Awesome, and you see it actually removes all the mistakes that I made

00:40.500 --> 00:42.000
and formatted it as an email.

00:42.600 --> 00:44.800
Sweet. And then we have Agent Mode.

00:44.900 --> 00:48.200
This essentially lets you trigger AI actions with your voice.

00:48.300 --> 00:53.700
You can either press command and speak, or click right here on the notch and type.

00:53.800 --> 00:58.400
This could be sending an email, scheduling an appointment,

00:58.500 --> 01:00.900
maybe getting some information from Notion,

01:01.000 --> 01:03.600
really anything that you can do in the integrations that we offer.

01:03.700 --> 01:07.600
And if you're ever unsure on how to use it or what apps you can connect to,

01:07.700 --> 01:08.900
you can simply ask VoiceOS.

01:09.000 --> 01:12.500
Hey, what are the apps that you can connect to?

01:13.500 --> 01:17.000
Let me check what I can connect to.

01:17.100 --> 01:19.600
Here is the card showing the apps I can connect to.

01:19.700 --> 01:22.100
Just click connect on any of them to link them up.

01:22.200 --> 01:23.500
Let me give an example with Gmail.

01:23.600 --> 01:25.900
Hey, can you send an email to Kai

01:26.000 --> 01:28.500
asking if he wants to grab some coffee tomorrow at 7pm?

01:33.100 --> 01:35.000
Drafting that email to Kai now.

01:35.400 --> 01:40.900
I drafted this email for you in Gmail. Take a look.

01:41.700 --> 01:42.300
Sweet.

01:42.400 --> 01:45.800
So another thing to note is that any of the sensitive actions,

01:45.900 --> 01:49.000
this could be sending an email, scheduling an appointment,

01:49.100 --> 01:53.500
creating a Notion document, not getting it, would have this confirmation.

01:53.700 --> 01:57.500
This is to make sure that nothing gets sent without your explicit confirmation.

01:58.000 --> 01:59.200
So in this case, this looks good.

01:59.300 --> 02:00.500
Let's do it.

02:01.600 --> 02:05.000
I have sent the email to Kai.

02:05.800 --> 02:06.800
Awesome.

02:07.100 --> 02:09.200
And then the last thing would be this side notch.

02:09.300 --> 02:11.900
You can find it on the left here by clicking it.

02:12.200 --> 02:15.900
And this essentially is just a history of every interaction you've had with VoiceOS.

02:16.600 --> 02:20.400
And it lets you kind of move back and forth between tasks while staying in flow.

02:20.500 --> 02:24.500
Super handy for revisiting all the information.

02:25.000 --> 02:27.000
All right, I think that's it for this overview. Thanks!
